    <div class="article-body">
      <div class="article-summary-box"><strong>Quick Answer:</strong> Vernal, Utah is the gateway to Dinosaur National Monument and the heart of Utah's Uintah Basin — a compact adventure hub where you can touch real 149-million-year-old dinosaur fossils, ride red-rock canyons on a guided UTV tour, walk up to thousand-year-old petroglyphs, and fish alpine reservoirs, all within an hour of downtown. Give it two to three days: one for the monument and rock art, one for a backcountry UTV tour and the state parks, and an optional third for Flaming Gorge, fishing, or the high Uintas. The best months are May–June and September–October. It delivers much of what draws people to southern Utah, with a fraction of the crowds.</div>

      <div class="key-takeaways">
        <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul>
